# ⏱️ WORK & TIME 

==================================================

## Core Relations
Work = Efficiency × Time  
Efficiency = Work / Time  
Efficiency ∝ 1 / Time  
Time ∝ 1 / Efficiency  

==================================================

## Individual Work
If A completes work in x days:  
Efficiency of A = 1/x  

If B completes work in y days:  
Efficiency of B = 1/y  

==================================================

## Combined Work
A & B together = (x × y) / (x + y)  

A, B, C together = 1 / (1/x + 1/y + 1/z)  

Total efficiency = Σ(1/individual time)  

==================================================

## LCM Method
Total work = LCM of individual times  

Work per day = Total work / Individual time  

Time = Total work / Total efficiency  

==================================================

## Partial Work
Work done = Time × Efficiency  

Remaining work = Total work − Work done  

==================================================

## Ratio Concept
Efficiency ratio = a : b  

Time ratio = b : a  

==================================================

## Wages Based Problems
Wages ∝ Work done  

Work done = Efficiency × Time  

Wage ratio = (Efficiency₁ × Time₁) : (Efficiency₂ × Time₂)  

==================================================

## Alternate Days Work
Work in 2 days = Efficiency(A) + Efficiency(B)  

Total days = Total work / Work in 2 days  

==================================================

## Pipes & Cisterns
Filling pipe → +ve efficiency  

Emptying pipe → −ve efficiency  

Net efficiency = Σ(inlets) − Σ(outlets)  

Time = 1 / Net efficiency  

==================================================

## Men–Days–Hours
Work ∝ Men × Days × Hours  

M₁ × D₁ × H₁ = M₂ × D₂ × H₂  

==================================================

## Efficiency Change
If efficiency increases by k%:  
New efficiency = (100 + k)/100  
New time = Old time × 100 / (100 + k)  

If efficiency decreases by k%:  
New efficiency = (100 − k)/100  
New time = Old time × 100 / (100 − k)  

==================================================

## Standard Results
Efficiency ∝ Work done  

Time ∝ 1 / Efficiency  

A & B together = xy / (x + y)  

==================================================

## Special Cases
If A is k times efficient as B:  
Time ratio = 1 : k  

If A works p days and B works q days:  
Total work = p(1/x) + q(1/y)  



